# A pump refuses, by name, an inlet that is not a liquid (DEV.md 4c C188 defect 2).
# Former gate: check_pump_liquid_inlet.py.  rotating/Pump.cpp is the incompressible
# pump, W = v dP / eta on the LIQUID molar volume; it never read its inlet's phase,
# so a vapour was "pumped" and came out liquid at exit 0.  (a) pump01 (water) fed
# at 400 K and 1 bar resolves to vapour: the run must exit non-zero saying it is not
# a liquid and naming the compressor.  (b) pump01 itself still runs.
# NOT checked: a produced two-phase inlet (no corpus case feeds a pump one).
group      pump-liquid-inlet
row        pump-liquid-inlet
binary     choupoSolve
base       tutorials/steady/rotating/pump01_water
strip      constant/propertyManifest expected
ok_head    "check_pump_liquid_inlet: OK -- "
fail_head  "check_pump_liquid_inlet: FAILED"
bullet     plain
ok_tail    .  NOT checked: a produced two-phase inlet (no corpus case feeds a pump one)

probe      (a) water fed at 400 K and 1 bar
  edit     0/feed	re:^T\s+298\.15 K;	T               400 K;
  match    is not a liquid
  match    compressor
  ok       a vapour inlet (water, 400 K, 1 bar) is refused, naming the compressor

control    (b) pump01 itself
  ok       pump01 (liquid water) runs as before
